{"baseRefName":"main","baseRefOid":"7396d7d316ab72957bca9709483f4638daa0d5cb","body":"Validate a pending payment with one heterogeneous await condition: documentObserved is true and approvedAmount covers the captured amount. Four ordinary observations exercise start, each condition alone, then both together. Separate false events retain the exact actual continuation; they do not accumulate into permission to release payment.\n\nThree tests passed at `e0d0b4c7e80f53ead164358a68d804dc18c68d89` (tree `c1701271cd6afc56092fab416137505aa68d31a8`) in53.648905 seconds including the cold SDK-free build. Comparisons cover the whole Program/filled Plan, four entire library reports, four real CLI outputs including exact ASCII bytes/empty stderr/exit, and actual continuation/frame/state linkage. All49 independently frozen fixture files are unchanged. Attempted work is5/6/6/10; committed work is5/5/5/15.\n\nThe source uses existing adopted Core2 behavior; production and dependencies are unchanged. The consumer alone was formatted. Two immutable normative blank-EOF copies retain exact frozen bytes. Fresh independent ordinary review approves the exact formatted source and actual result, and explicitly supports the finite integration after PR216: merge parents `7396d7d`/`7ef60cd`, composition tree `2e7037c`, all36 pinned upstream changes, all50 unchanged incoming paths, and combined tree `f18c2346ff435f9ac95a7f6f56457c2edde3f71c`. Root verified those guards against actual main `2d8632ecd48e21a98fb9efc823fe68296a59dfec`. The combined tree itself was not re-executed.\n\nDocument and amount observations are local caller-supplied values with no authentication or consumption tracking. This does not implement cancellation, compensation, proof or ledger delivery, and all14 original staged gaps and broader acceptance exits remain open.\n","files":[{"path":"crates/fixtures/core2-multi-condition-complete/BYTE-FACTS.json","additions":36,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"crates/fixtu